**Poolside Keydown** (PK) is a dialect of [[keydown]] written for Waterflow. It has its own marks, its own way of formatting and its own styles: headings start with lane marks, lists use rings, chips are written as angle tags such as `<ring words>`, and every one of them is drawn with an original design (life rings, lane ropes, buoys, pool tiles and drops) in the [[poolside-style|Poolside style]]: clear cyan and blue water with crisp orange.

Poolside Keydown is translated to and from ordinary Keydown, so nothing is lost. The Keydown engine draws it, a note can be switched between the two at any time, and exporting a note as a `.kd` file writes plain Keydown that [[radii-office|Writeout and Bitbook]] can open.

## Where to use it
* **In Waterflow**, every new note is written in Poolside Keydown (Settings has a choice for new notes, and the note's menu switches a single note).
* **Anywhere else** that draws Keydown (Writeout, Bitbook, this page and Keydown.js), wrap Poolside Keydown in `;;pk{ }`. It works as a block, on one line or over several, and as words inside a sentence.

;;pk{/ A block of Poolside Keydown
<< Written between the braces of a block.
() Lists, quotes, chips and dividers all work in it.
<ring Chips> and <foam more chips> too.}

A sentence can hold ;;pk{<sun a chip>} or ;;pk{<neon a neon sign>} written the same way.

## Headings
A heading starts with slashes, one for each level, and a space.

;;pk{/ / A big title
// // A section
/// /// A small heading}

## Quotes and callouts
`<<` starts a quiet quote. `<` followed by one of Keydown's quote marks makes a callout, so `<!` is an alert, `<?` is a question and `<>` is a pulled quote.

;;pk{<< << A quiet quote, a tile with an orange edge.
<! <! Heads up: an alert with a life ring.
<? <? A question to think about.
<> <> A pulled quote between two lane ropes.}

## Lists
A list item starts with a ring, written `()`. A mark inside the ring chooses the marker.

;;pk{() () A life ring
(+) (+) A water drop
(.) (.) A bubble
(~) (~) An orange tile
(=) (=) A wave chevron}

## Text styles
`<b words>` is bold and `<i words>` is italic, drawn in deep blue and orange.

;;pk{Some <b bold words> and <i italic words>.}

## Chips
A chip is an angle tag with a name and the words it holds: `<name words>`. There are forty, and each has its own look.

### Rings, ropes and floats
* `<ring words>` is a striped life ring: ;;pk{<ring ring>}
* `<lap words>` has a lane rope under it: ;;pk{<lap lap>}
* `<reef words>` has a wave under it: ;;pk{<reef reef>}
* `<buoy words>` is an orange float: ;;pk{<buoy buoy>}
* `<hoop words>` is rings inside rings: ;;pk{<hoop hoop>}
* `<dots words>` is a dotted lane line: ;;pk{<dots dots>}
* `<cone words>` is a cone, orange and white stripes: ;;pk{<cone cone>}

### Water and light
* `<foam words>` is sea foam full of bubbles: ;;pk{<foam foam>}
* `<bubble words>` is a round bubble with a shine: ;;pk{<bubble bubble>}
* `<pearl words>` is a pearl: ;;pk{<pearl pearl>}
* `<drop words>` is a water drop: ;;pk{<drop drop>}
* `<splash words>` is a splash with flying drops: ;;pk{<splash splash>}
* `<lagoon words>` is shaded water in a double frame: ;;pk{<lagoon lagoon>}
* `<mist words>` is a patch of mist: ;;pk{<mist mist>}
* `<beam words>` is an underwater light beam: ;;pk{<beam beam>}
* `<lens words>` is a glass lens: ;;pk{<lens lens>}
* `<frost words>` is frosted glass: ;;pk{<frost frost>}
* `<shimmer words>` is water shimmer with an orange edge: ;;pk{<shimmer shimmer>}
* `<neon words>` is a blue neon sign: ;;pk{<neon neon>}
* `<sun words>` is a sun with rays: ;;pk{<sun sun>}

### Signs, flags and badges
* `<deep words>` is the deep end, with a waterline on top: ;;pk{<deep deep>}
* `<tile words>` is a square of pool tile: ;;pk{<tile tile>}
* `<sign words>` is a pool sign with an orange header: ;;pk{<sign sign>}
* `<pennant words>` is a pennant: ;;pk{<pennant pennant>}
* `<banner words>` is a swallowtail banner: ;;pk{<banner banner>}
* `<tab words>` is a folder tab: ;;pk{<tab tab>}
* `<badge words>` is a lifeguard badge with a cross: ;;pk{<badge badge>}
* `<pass words>` is a pool pass: ;;pk{<pass pass>}
* `<say words>` is a speech bubble: ;;pk{<say say>}
* `<capsule words>` is a two-tone capsule: ;;pk{<capsule capsule>}
* `<split words>` is a chip split in two tones: ;;pk{<split split>}

### Marks and inks
* `<halo words>` and `<sunhalo words>` glow: ;;pk{<halo halo> <sunhalo sunhalo>}
* `<mark words>` and `<flag words>` are highlighter strokes: ;;pk{<mark mark> <flag flag>}
* `<ink words>` and `<fire words>` look written with a pen: ;;pk{<ink ink> <fire fire>}
* `<under words>`, `<strike words>` and `<frame words>` underline, strike through and frame: ;;pk{<under under> <strike strike> <frame frame>}

## Blanks and practice boxes
`<blank 8|answer>` is a blank to write in, eight characters wide, with the answer hidden until it is clicked, and `<box 6>` is the same as an empty box. `(_ box|3|Write here _)` leaves room to write.

;;pk{Water is <blank 8|wet> and a box is <box 6>.
(_ box|2|Write here _)}

## Dividers
`/~ style | Title | color` draws a divider. The styles are `rope`, `lane`, `tile`, `wave`, `reef`, `step`, `ring`, `glass`, `buoy` and `water`, and the colors are `cyan`, `blue` and `orange`.

;;pk{/~ rope | rope | blue
/~ lane | lane | cyan
/~ tile | tile | orange
/~ wave | wave | blue
/~ reef | reef | cyan
/~ step | step | blue
/~ ring | ring | orange
/~ glass | glass | cyan
/~ buoy | buoy | orange
/~ water | water | blue}

## Everything else is Keydown
Poolside Keydown has no marks for tables, equations or code fences, so those are written the [[keydown|Keydown]] way inside it, and any Keydown tag works too. A note keeps its own language, so a Classic Keydown note and a Poolside Keydown note can sit side by side in Waterflow.

## How it translates
Each Poolside mark stands for exactly one Keydown mark, so the translation goes both ways.

* `/ Title` is `# Title`
* `<< quote` is `> quote`, and `<! alert` is `!> alert`
* `() item` is `- item`, and `(+) item` is `+ item`
* `<b words>` is `**words**`, and `<i words>` is `*words*`
* `<ring words>` is `!!:O#words#`
* `<foam words>` is `#C#words#`
* `<sun words>` is `++O~words++`

A blank is `<blank 8|answer>` in Poolside Keydown and `[__8|answer]` in Keydown, and a divider is `/~ rope | Title | blue` in Poolside Keydown and `::divider{poolside|Title|blue}` in Keydown.

The translator is `poolside.js`, and the styles are `poolside-keydown.css` (and `poolside-embed.css` for `;;pk{ }` blocks). See also [[poolside-style]], [[poolsideui]] and [[keydown-components]].
